What leads a person to be attracted to his own sex?
At first, infants perceive themselves as a whole with their mother, but between about two and four years of life, the process of determining sex begins. At this stage of development, the boy will need to separate from his unity with his mother and establish a deeper connection with his father, because it is through relations with him that he learns what it means to be a man.
What are they doing?
At the age of about 6 years, when children begin to go to school, a new stage begins: now the boy looks at his peers in search of answers to the same questions that his father had before. He seeks to be accepted and recognized by other boys.
It should be remembered that a sensitive temperament alone does not make a person homosexual, only in combination with certain environmental factors can he contribute to the development of same-sex attraction. It is also important not so much the father himself as the fatherly figure, i.e.
