Copiapoa atacamensis
La Copiapoa atacamensis It is a species of globular cactus, solitary or branched, grayish-green in color, and spiny. The spines are black or brown, depending on the variety.
La Copiapoa coquimbana, known as coquimbano, is a plant with a greenish and globose-cylindrical body that tends to form clumps up to 1 meter high. The spines are black when young, then gray.
La Copiapoa humilis or humildito is a branched cactus with a globose-cylindrical body of a brown-violet or greenish color depending on the subspecies. Reaches a height of about 20 centimeters, and its flowers are yellow and somewhat odorous.
La Copiapoa mollicula, called lowland in its place of origin, is a kind of branched cactus, with a greenish body, with black spines. Grows up to 10 centimeters tall.
