How do I know if my cactus is rotting?
One of the questions we ask ourselves the most, especially when we start, is the following: How do i know if my cactus is rotting?
Well, the truth is that as in everything in this life, it depends. What does it depend on?
But ... what happens if you are not getting the amount of light you need or you are not watering properly? In these cases, the cactus softens.
Excess irrigation: the roots die suffocated and the fleshy body of the plant rots quickly.
What to do to avoid it?
Use a substrate that has very good drainage, either pumice, black peat mixed with perlite in equal parts, or similar.
Another option is to take the pot before watering and again after a few days. As the dry substrate does not weigh the same as when it is wet, it can serve as an orientation.
If you have doubts, do not leave them in the inkwell. Question .
