Therefore, one of the first things to do when buying a plant is to choose a pot for it. It is possible - although rare - that you do not need it at that precise moment, but the normal thing is that when they go from the producer to the nursery facilities the cacti are well rooted.
Terracotta pots are ideal for cacti, and indeed for almost all types of plants (except carnivorous ones). The reason is that as they are porous, the roots have a better grip, and that ends up being seen in the root ball or soil bread, as well as in the plant itself.
Octagonal pots are especially suitable for cacti that tend to produce many shoots, like many Mammillaria, Lobivia or Rebutia for example. The ones we show you They are hard plastic, and feature your plate.
These are in assorted colors (pink, light blue, green, yellowish, white, pink, lilac and cream), and a plate is also included for each one. They are the most interesting because their drainage system is formed by multiple holes in the base of each container., the ideal size so that the water can flow out quickly but at the same time to prevent the soil from being lost quickly, which is the case with pots that have large holes.
These original and decorative cactus pots will beautify the place where you are going to put them. They are shaped like an owl, with large eyes and the drawing of feathers.
If you have a little overgrown cacti and you are looking for somewhat larger pots to plant in them, then we recommend these. They measure 8 centimeters in diameter and high, so they are perfect for your plants since they also have a hole in their base so that any excess water comes out.
