Cacti are succulent plants that have managed to conquer the hearts and lives of more than one person. They are so popular that it is hard to believe that many species have such a low price, something that only fuels our curiosity and desire to have more specimens.
Pangea was a supercontinent in the process of being divided by the movement of tectonic plates (the »puzzle pieces» that make up planet Earth), that enjoyed a warm climate. As earthquakes and volcanic eruptions divided it, each of the continents that we know today headed towards their current locations.
But the most dramatic change was the replacement of leaves by thorns, which are actually leaf spines (hence, for example, when inadvertently we pluck one, after a while another sprouts again). They could no longer photosynthesize through them, but there was no problem: the stem started to produce chlorophyll, and as a consequence, it turned green.
Succulents, or non-cacti succulents, are plants that appeared after cacti, when the "piece" that is today the African continent was locating itself, always little by little and over the course of millions of years, in its current situation. Now, unfortunately, it is not known exactly when the crass began their evolution.
