3 What are the benefits of diatomaceous earth?
It is a siliceous mineral formed by fossilized microscopic algae. When the algae die, their organic content is destroyed, leaving only their silica skeleton which is deposited at the bottom of the water.
How does it act? What every grain of diatomaceous earth does is penetrate the body of the parasite, insect, or small animal (like the snail) that is damaging the plants, thus causing them to die of dehydration.
