Iron ore prices soared, hitting a new high in nearly 8 years
On December 21, the closing price of the main iron ore futures contract reached 1144.5 yuan/ton, a record high since iron ore futures were listed in 2013. On the same day, the China Iron Ore Price Index (CIOPI) imported iron ore price index reached 602.55 points, and the price of 62% direct imported iron ore reached US$171.92/ton, both hitting new highs in the past 8 years.
