News - Reasons and solutions for bridging in welding in PCBA processing
Reasons and solutions for bridging in welding in PCBA processing News
PCB printed circuit board design: Strictly carry out scientific planning at the circuit board design level, reasonably distribute the weight of components on both sides, open air holes and through holes, adjust the spacing of dense components, and appropriately add solder mask layers etc.
Reflow oven temperature curve: In PCBA processing, in a literal sense, when the liquid solder is melted, the solder at the higher temperature end is more active. If the reflow soldering temperature profile is set unreasonably, it will cause disordered flow of solder paste and increase the probability of bridging.
Choose a solder paste inkjet printer: A solder paste inkjet printer does not need to apply solder paste through a stencil, which will reduce the solder paste contact caused by unscientific module openings, steel warpage, and stencil separation. Poor coating.
Reasonable control of the amount of solder paste: Reasonable control of the amount of solder paste applied to reduce the problem of excessive collapse of the solder paste and high fluidity.
