The solution to PCBA processing through tin PCBA processing through tin is mainly affected by materials, wave soldering process, flux, manual soldering and other factors, which can be adjusted and solved by the following methods:
The tin melted at high temperature has strong permeability, but not all welded metals (PCB boards, components) can penetrate in, such as aluminum metal, its surface generally automatically forms a dense protective layer, and the internal molecules The difference in structure also makes it difficult for other molecules to penetrate. Second, if there is an oxide layer on the surface of the metal to be welded, it will also prevent the penetration of molecules.
