Why do PCBA testing? What are the main contents of PCBA test?
The PCBA test mainly includes the adjustment of circuit parameters, that is, the adjustment of the adjustable components of the PCBA, the tuning system related to the electrical indicators, and the mechanical transmission part to make them meet the predetermined performance requirements. On the basic theory of adjustment, systematically test the technical indicators of the whole machine to make the technical indicators of the finished PCBA meet the specified requirements.
Clarify the purpose and requirements of PCBA testing.
Select and use test instruments correctly and reasonably.
Adjust and test the PCBA according to the test process.
Use the basic theoretical knowledge of circuits and components to analyze and eliminate faults in debugging.
Analyze and process PCBA test data.
Write a test summary based on the test results, and put forward suggestions for PCBA processing improvement.
The PCBA test work is generally carried out in the assembly workshop and is carried out in strict accordance with the test process. For more complex large-scale equipment, according to the design requirements, part of the test work or rough adjustment can be carried out in the production plant, and then the final installation and comprehensive test work can be carried out in the installation site or experimental base according to the requirements of the technical documents.
