History of PCB development in the world
In 1943, the Americans used the technology within military radios.
In 1948, the United States officially recognized the invention and used for commercial purposes.
The 1960s of the 20th world, the realization of hole metallization double-sided PCB to achieve mass production.
In the 1980s, surface-mounted printed circuit boards (SMT) gradually replaced the cartridge PCBs and became the mainstream of production.
Since the 21st century, high-density BGA, chip-level packaging and organic laminate materials for the substrate of multi-chip module packaging printed circuit board has been developed rapidly.
