How to deal with the problem that the wheels of the truck cannot return to the right position automatically after steering?
The righting effect of kingpin caster is related to vehicle speed, while the righting effect of kingpin caster is almost independent of vehicle speed. Therefore, when the car is running at high speed, the righting effect of backward tilt is greater than that of inward tilt at low speed.
Knowing this principle, let's analyze the reason why the steering wheel of this truck will not return to the right position by itself. To be sure, there is something wrong with the steering wheel alignment of this truck.
The common faults are: the plane bearing of the knuckle pin is damaged, the knuckle pin sleeve is excessively worn (that is, the "vertical shaft" is broken), the bearing of the steering wheel is loose or damaged, and the knuckle is deformed. In addition, broken front bow piece, broken center screw, too loose riding bolt, broken bow shaft, etc.
Another possibility is that the bearings and sleeves of the knuckle pin and the steering ball head are poorly lubricated, which leads to excessive resistance of the steering wheel alignment, and this situation also leads to the failure of the steering wheel alignment. At this time, just lubricate these parts.
